+## What this records
+
+**ADR 069: the plan is where the product model meets the work.** Accepted by the product owner on 2026-11-12 through /design-adr. It retires ADRs 049 and 057.
+
+- **The model knows only the business.** It holds no reference to plans, epics, tracker issues or the tracker, and no decision records. Links run one way, from the work to the model.
+- **Where decisions live.** A product decision is the person's answer, kept as the content of the part it decides. An ADR records a decision about the code.
+- **A plan** holds one or more slices of its business intent, plus chores. It has **one Epic** and **one eval**. A done plan lands on main only when its eval passes. Until the eval runner exists (#801), the Garura harness runs the eval by hand.
+- **The plan tracks its slices** and their status. /reshape-plan gets "add a slice". The unplanned epic goes.
+
+Refs #954
+
+## How to review it
+
+- `docs/adr/069-...md`: the record (272 lines).
+- ADRs 049 and 057: marked "Superseded by ADR 069".
+- 14 older ADRs: one forward pointer each on the Status line.
+- `docs/adr/_index.md`: rebuilt.
+- Everything else is run records, including copies of the ontology and the ADR template kept as evidence.
+- No model file, play or skill changes here. The ADR lists that work under "Work This Creates": the ontology change, the model clean-up, the /shape-plan and /design-eval rework, and the /reshape-plan changes.
+
