+shape: markdown
+number: 069
+title_hint: 'The Plan Is Where the Product Model Meets the Work: the Model Knows No Plan, No Tracker and No Decision Record, One Epic and One Eval for Each Plan, and a Done Plan Lands on Main Only When Its Eval Passes'
+status: proposed
+level: framework
+date: 2026-11-12
+decided_in: '#954 (/shape-plan makes an Epic for each slice; a plan should have one Epic that holds all its slices)'
+template_path: .garura/project/issues/_adr/20261112T093635Z/context/templates/standards/templates/adr.md
+draft_path: .garura/project/issues/_adr/20261112T093635Z/adr-draft.md
+round: 5
+memory_copies:
+  ontology_from_memory: .garura/project/issues/_adr/20261112T093635Z/context/memory/standards/schemas/product-os/ontology.md
+  note: Line numbers are read from the source ontology, core/components/memory/standards/schemas/product-os/ontology.md, version 16. Phoenix memory's copy is version 15.
+changes_at_acceptance:
+- '1. Until an eval runner exists, the Garura harness runs the plan''s eval by hand before a done plan lands. The runner is #801 (/validate-epic runs the hidden evals and the checks, and gives the verdict, under #800). #819 is closed and is no longer named as the runner. Round-1 point 1 (ADR 060) is settled: only a done plan waits for its eval; a paused plan still merges (ADR 060 §2).'
+- '2. NEW principle, its own numbered part, early: the product model holds no reference to plans, epics, tracker issues or the tracker. Links run one way, from the work side (plans, tracker issues, evals, hidden files) to the model. A slice does not name its plan, the plan''s folder or its eval; the plan names its slices. The business intent page''s Tracker line goes (reverses the last sentence of ADR 068 §1).'
+- '3. Round-1 point 3 settled: what replaces the per-slice eval index file (and the eval and guide layout) is left to the /design-eval rework.'
+- '4. Round-1 point 4 settled: a slice is in progress when the plan file that holds it records it so. The plan file records each slice it holds and that slice''s status. The model is not asked.'
+- '5. Round-1 point 5 settled: /reshape-plan gets an ''add a slice'' instruction for a plan that exists.'
+- '6. Round-1 point 6 settled: the unplanned epic goes. A plan''s chores sit in the plan, under its one epic.'
+second_change_at_acceptance:
+- A. The record states the principle and changes no business intent page itself. The change to the Business Intent kind (no Tracker line; What was done links to no work item) is made through /specify-ontology with the product owner's checkpoints, and is listed under Work This Creates. Affects names the ontology's Business Intent kind, not the intent pages or ids. No intent's title, outcome, why, asked by, proof, must not, rules or stage changes.
+- 'B. Round-2 open point 1 settled: each plan''s eval covers every feature of its slices, the held_by ones included; each plan file records that slice''s status for itself.'
+- 'C. Round-2 open point 2 settled: existing ids (bi-<n>, fn-<n>) stay as names. Later work: a new business intent gets an id that does not come from the tracker.'
+- 'D. Round-2 open point 3 settled: every reference to the tracker and to plans is removed from the model, including pages that cite tracker issue numbers as sources and the spine''s created_by / updated_by lines that name an issue. Git history keeps the origin and is not changed. The clean-up is Work This Creates, through product-os-keeper and the model''s skills, and needs a new ontology rule.'
+reference_definition: A "reference" is a name, number, link, path or field in the model (a page and its Sources, a spine entry and its metadata, a slice record) that points at one particular plan, plan folder, eval, hidden file, epic or tracker issue, or at the tracker. Cited issue numbers ("#946", "Built (#818)") and created_by / updated_by lines that name an issue count (settled at acceptance). A part whose subject is plans may still describe plans in general, with placeholders (ADR 065 rule 3, last sentence, kept; the product owner said "ok to your proposal"). Seven Garura pages describe the plan files that way (for example fn-818 line 11, "`.garura/project/plans/<intent>.yaml`"); the keeper reads them as descriptions, not references.
+supersedes:
+- adr: 049
+  part: full
+  why: 'The product owner retires it. What goes: one epic for each slice, one epic shared by two plans, one eval for each slice. Every other part, as amended by ADR 052, ADR 057, ADR 063, ADR 067 and ADR 068, is restated (Decision §9), phrased from the plan''s side so that no restated part has the model know a plan.'
+- adr: '057'
+  part: full
+  why: 'The product owner retires it. What goes: the slice file eval.<slice-id>.md and the eval as the slice''s. §1, §2, §4 to §7, as amended by ADR 068, are restated (Decision §10).'
+amends:
+- adr: 048
